rmative  or negative if there is a negative vote  it requires a comment  as a technical concern regarding  the proposed standard  if there are no negatives  the ballot with the proposed ballot item  with the proposed  standard moves on the main committee  ballot however  if there are any negatives the rules of  the balloting process  state that all negatives must be  resolved  before it can move on to the main  committee ballot  so if there is a negative  the technical contact  for the work item works to resolve any  negatives  and comments and then  there's a decision tree  if the negative comment is persuasive  but it is a change that is not editorial  then the standard is revised and sent  back to the  subcommittee for rebalancing  if through the resolution process  that proposed or required change  concerning the negative is an editorial  or if the negative is withdrawn after  discussion  or in the worst case  if the negative voter refuses to work  with the technical contact in resolving  that  the negative vote  it is possible to find  the negative vote non-persuasive  that process requires presentation of  uh adjudication at a stated meeting  during the june meeting or the december  meeting  so if the vote is editorial  and can move on or if the negative vote  is withdrawn or if it's found  non-persuasive then it can move on  to main committee for balloting  the main committee balloting process  requires  30 days and again it goes through the  same process  during the balloting process if you have  negative votes and comments they have to  be addressed  and the same decision tree is used  to resolve negatives as in the one that  was described for the subcommittee  if there are no negative votes it  me it moved the standard test method  moves on to the committee on standards  for review and then  published after that  so the big question as i mentioned most  people have  regarding astm standards and and some  other  standard development organizations it  takes 