e that the goal  is to develop the new procedure  for the additional components and  incorporate  the new procedure as procedure b  with the current procedure in d7845  as procedure a i am currently  collaborating with intertek  on that work  then we also have uh some joint work  with bureau veritas as  we revise astm  d8110 at present  d8110 was published with conditional  provisional precision data  and it's for the elemental analysis of  metal distillates by icp mass spec  the goal is to expand the scope of the  element table capabilities  and to include crude oil analysis by icp  mass spec  so those are the standard test methods  that i am working  on and moving at  astm  so one note and to make sure  the information that i provided is based  on my experience  and the resources that i have at  astm.org  i would recommend and suggest  that you join astm  possibly attend the biennial meetings if  you're interested in participating  and also and more important as you  might have noticed there's a significant  amount of work  performed by the task groups and as  as a technical contact for multiple  standards  it is uh challenging to find  participating labs  and i and i truly understand why because  i've managed laboratories  in the past at contract labs and  i know the volume of work that is  performed  in most laboratories  it makes it difficult to add additional  load of sample testing  to participate in an ils but  it's vitally important to continue to  expand the volunteer list  so that we can have additional support  and resources that help to develop  standards  so you can go to the website astm.org  and get all of the details required  beyond  what i obviously have provided here  and in closing the disclaimer is that  this is not inclusive of what  is required to establish a standard it  is merely  an overview and if you need  additional details you may contact  the staff at astm.org  thank you for your time today i believe  we're moving on to the questions 